{
	"children": [
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#ffd400",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[359.456,208.737,555.9,217.703],[339.229,198.279,555.894,207.245],[339.229,187.821,555.903,196.787],[339.229,177.353,416.947,186.32]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|003775|00595",
			"annotationText": "The choice of optimization technique is key to the efficiency of the learner, and also helps determine the classifier produced if the evaluation function has more than one optimum.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:14:50Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:14:50Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "2J3TTVWC",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#5fb236",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "4",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":3,\"rects\":[[53.802,725.993,292.882,734.96],[53.802,715.535,292.892,724.502]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00003|000052|00067",
			"annotationText": "Cross-validation can help to combat overfitting, for example by using it to choose the best size of decision tree to learn.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:30:16Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:30:16Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "36A7FA9T",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#e56eee",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "3",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":2,\"rects\":[[484.746,403.172,555.906,412.138],[316.809,392.705,555.916,401.671],[316.809,382.246,555.89,391.213],[316.809,371.788,373.822,380.755]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00002|003242|00390",
			"annotationText": "Bias is a learner’s tendency to consistently learn the same wrong thing. Variance is the tendency to learn random things irrespective of the real signal",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:01:53Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:01:53Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "67V2P7R8",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#2ea8e5",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[108.685,281.664,168.213,290.63]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|001395|00501",
			"annotationText": "folk knowledge",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T16:39:14Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T16:39:14Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "6YFYVCC8",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"charset": "",
			"contentType": "application/pdf",
			"dateAdded": "2025-05-06T20:13:25Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-08-21T19:37:24Z",
			"filename": "Domingos - 2012 - A few useful things to know about machine learning.pdf",
			"itemType": "attachment",
			"key": "72QKGZWL",
			"linkMode": "imported_file",
			"parentItem": "57DT53SS",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": [],
			"title": "PDF"
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#f19837",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "3",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":2,\"rects\":[[431.621,361.321,555.911,370.288],[316.809,350.863,555.912,359.83],[316.809,340.405,470.444,349.371]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00002|003441|00432",
			"annotationText": "A linear learner has high bias, because when the frontier between two classes is not a hyperplane the learner is unable to induce it",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:21:28Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:21:28Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "7T8MQSM4",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#2ea8e5",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "3",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":2,\"rects\":[[449.469,486.855,555.938,495.821],[316.809,476.396,555.935,485.363],[316.809,465.938,555.922,474.905],[316.809,455.471,537.826,464.437]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00002|002882|00296",
			"annotationText": "When your learner outputs a classifier that is 100% accurate on the training data but only 50% accurate on test data, when in fact it could have output one that is 75% accurate on both, it has overfit",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:57:18Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:57:18Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "8WAIK9LI",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#5fb236",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "3",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":2,\"rects\":[[316.809,413.63,555.911,422.596],[316.809,403.172,478.103,412.138]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00002|003140|00369",
			"annotationText": "One way to understand overfitting is by decomposing generalization error into bias and variance [9]",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:01:23Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:01:23Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "98VANY87",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#a28ae5",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "2",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":1,\"rects\":[[320.139,263.385,555.916,272.351],[316.809,252.927,531.502,261.893]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00001|003293|00519",
			"annotationText": "n the early days of machine learning, the need to keep training and test data separate was not widely appreciated",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:29:38Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:29:38Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "9PB5VEKK",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#e56eee",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[340.465,72.451,555.917,81.417]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|004242|00710",
			"annotationText": "Decision trees test one feature at each internal node,",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:16:37Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:16:37Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "AHQ67Y52",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#a28ae5",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[373.608,305.794,555.939,314.76],[339.229,295.336,555.959,304.302],[339.229,284.878,457.995,293.844]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|003335|00487",
			"annotationText": "An evaluation function (also called objective function or scoring function) is needed to distinguish good classifiers from bad ones.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T17:01:10Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T17:01:10Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "AIFD77P4",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#f19837",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "2",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":1,\"rects\":[[53.802,239.823,292.923,248.789],[53.802,229.355,221.127,238.322]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00001|001625|00543",
			"annotationText": "The fundamental goal of machine learning is to generalize beyond the examples in the training set.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:12:54Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:12:54Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "B5VUHAJ8",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#e56eee",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "2",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":1,\"rects\":[[386.2,116.936,555.885,125.903],[316.809,106.469,555.886,115.436],[316.809,96.011,555.876,104.978],[316.809,85.554,459.765,94.52]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00001|003997|00676",
			"annotationText": "since the objective function is only a proxy for the true goal, we may not need to fully optimize it; in fact, a local optimum returned by simple greedy search may be better than the global optimum.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:32:05Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:32:05Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "B7S36RY5",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#f19837",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[153.641,489.384,194.691,498.35]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|000542|00293",
			"annotationText": "“black art",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T14:45:19Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T14:45:19Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "BAZ4JEWE",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#5fb236",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[257.487,177.057,292.933,186.023],[53.802,166.599,292.903,175.565],[53.802,156.132,292.914,165.098],[53.802,145.674,141.624,154.64]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|001873|00605",
			"annotationText": "A classifier is a system that inputs (typically) a vector of discrete and/or continuous feature values and outputs a single discrete value, the class.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T16:34:04Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T16:34:04Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "CB33AHZQ",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#f19837",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "4",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":3,\"rects\":[[182.632,156.132,292.89,165.099],[53.802,145.675,292.928,154.641],[53.802,135.216,292.915,144.183],[53.802,124.75,199.183,133.716]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00003|002448|00637",
			"annotationText": "This expression was coined by Bellman in 1961 to refer to the fact that many algorithms that work fine in low dimensions become intractable when the input is high-dimensional.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:37:13Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:37:13Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "D79UN7AJ",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#f19837",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "3",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":2,\"rects\":[[53.802,103.832,292.923,112.798],[53.802,93.365,237.941,102.331]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00002|002530|00679",
			"annotationText": "What if the knowledge and data we have are not sufficient to completely determine the correct classifier?",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:51:18Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:51:18Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "EW29SKPY",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#f19837",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "2",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":1,\"rects\":[[403.52,148.32,555.914,157.286],[316.809,137.853,533.013,146.819]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00001|003815|00634",
			"annotationText": "We have to use training error as a surrogate for test error, and this is fraught with danger.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:31:18Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:31:18Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "FEWZXDGJ",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#ff6666",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "4",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":3,\"rects\":[[104.626,663.236,292.951,672.202],[53.802,652.769,205.251,661.735]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00003|000253|00119",
			"annotationText": "The most popular one is adding a regularization term to the evaluation function.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:31:56Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:31:56Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "FIUN6YSA",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#f19837",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[397.54,473.113,555.895,482.079],[316.809,462.655,492.689,471.621]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|002699|00309",
			"annotationText": "There are literally thousands available, and hundreds more are published each year.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T16:49:32Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T16:49:32Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "FXYMAQCM",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#2ea8e5",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "3",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":2,\"rects\":[[61.025,715.04,296.666,724.007],[53.802,704.573,292.894,713.539]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00002|000022|00067",
			"annotationText": "eneralization being the goal has another major consequence: data alone is not enough, no matter how much of it you have.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:36:28Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:36:28Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "GEM6XE6B",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#ffd400",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "3",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":2,\"rects\":[[476.945,340.405,555.906,349.371],[316.809,329.947,555.923,338.913],[316.809,319.48,555.948,328.446],[316.809,309.022,352.397,317.988]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00002|003592|00463",
			"annotationText": "Decision trees don’t have this problem because they can represent any Boolean function, but on the other hand they can suffer from high variance:",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:21:42Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:21:42Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "GHA7XPSJ",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#ffd400",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "2",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":1,\"rects\":[[53.802,513.908,292.91,522.875],[53.802,503.451,127.651,512.417]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00001|000611|00269",
			"annotationText": "with one branch for each feature value, and have class predictions at the leaves.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:29:12Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:29:12Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "GT4AMEIL",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"charset": "",
			"contentType": "application/pdf",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T14:41:45Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T14:41:50Z",
			"filename": "Domingos - 2012 - A few useful things to know about machine learning.pdf",
			"itemType": "attachment",
			"key": "H99THKZZ",
			"linkMode": "imported_file",
