			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[506.519,103.833,555.937,112.799],[316.809,93.366,555.896,102.333],[316.809,82.909,555.939,91.875],[316.809,72.451,335.231,81.417]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|004185|00700",
			"annotationText": "Hyperplanebased methods form a linear combination of the features per class and predict the class with the highest-valued combination.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:16:29Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:16:29Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "U3BAN6D7",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#e56eee",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "4",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":3,\"rects\":[[211.583,652.769,292.894,661.735],[53.802,642.311,292.882,651.277],[53.802,631.853,204.225,640.82]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00003|000322|00130",
			"annotationText": "This can, for example, penalize classifiers with more structure, thereby favoring smaller ones with less room to overfit",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:32:18Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:32:18Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "V64EQEFQ",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#5fb236",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "3",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":2,\"rects\":[[394.83,497.312,555.908,506.279],[316.809,486.855,445.738,495.821]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00002|002819|00285",
			"annotationText": "This problem is called overfitting, and is the bugbear of machine learning.",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:56:46Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:56:46Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "V6I7F85Q",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#ffd400",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "1",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":0,\"rects\":[[180.866,354.888,292.891,363.854],[53.802,344.43,292.894,353.396],[53.802,333.972,101.96,342.938]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00000|001071|00438",
			"annotationText": "d placement, credit scoring, fraud detection, stock trading, drug design, and many other applications",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T16:41:02Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T16:41:02Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "VAISVFGP",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#2ea8e5",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "2",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":1,\"rects\":[[316.809,179.702,555.942,188.669],[316.809,169.235,555.903,178.202],[316.809,158.777,555.933,167.744],[316.809,148.32,399.618,157.286]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00001|003647|00603",
			"annotationText": "Notice that generalization being the goal has an interesting consequence for machine learning. Unlike in most other optimization problems, we don’t have access to the function we want to optimize!",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T18:30:57Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T18:30:57Z",
			"itemType": "annotation",
			"key": "XDL9KAKL",
			"parentItem": "H99THKZZ",
			"relations": {},
			"tags": []
		},
		{
			"annotationAuthorName": "",
			"annotationColor": "#5fb236",
			"annotationComment": "",
			"annotationPageLabel": "4",
			"annotationPosition": "{\"pageIndex\":3,\"rects\":[[210.825,631.853,292.87,640.82],[53.802,621.386,292.883,630.353],[53.802,610.928,141.854,619.895]]}",
			"annotationSortIndex": "00003|000442|00161",
			"annotationText": "Another option is to perform a statistical significance test like chi-square before adding new structure,",
			"annotationType": "highlight",
			"dateAdded": "2025-04-03T19:32:47Z",
			"dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:32:47Z",
