		"abstractNote": "Machine learning algorithms can ﬁgure out how to perform important tasks by generalizing from examples. This is often feasible and cost-eﬀective where manual programming is not. As more data becomes available, more ambitious problems can be tackled. As a result, machine learning is widely used in computer science and other ﬁelds. However, developing successful machine learning applications requires a substantial amount of “black art” that is hard to ﬁnd in textbooks. This article summarizes twelve key lessons that machine learning researchers and practitioners have learned. These include pitfalls to avoid, important issues to focus on, and answers to common questions.",
